{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ML-05 — Feature Vector and Leakage/Privacy Check\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook builds the feature vector for the FlyRank starter dataset and attacks it for leakage. The target is `is_declining_label = (trend_direction == 'down')`. The intended use is a static, export-time prioritisation task; this is not a causal or future-month forecast.\n",
    "\n",
    "The safe rule is simple: identifiers, the target, fields used to compute the target, and workflow metadata do not enter the model. Features whose measurement window overlaps the label window are marked as snapshot features, not evidence of a future causal effect."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load the starter data\n",
    "\n",
    "Load the repository CSV without assuming the notebook's current working directory. The checks below use the raw columns, before the preparation script's blanket fills."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "candidate_paths = [\n",
    "    Path.cwd() / 'data' / 'raw' / 'content_refresh_anonymized.csv',\n",
    "    Path.cwd().parent / 'data' / 'raw' / 'content_refresh_anonymized.csv',\n",
    "    Path.cwd().parent.parent / 'data' / 'raw' / 'content_refresh_anonymized.csv',\n",
    "    Path.cwd() / 'content_refresh_anonymized.csv',\n",
    "]\n",
    "data_path = next((p for p in candidate_paths if p.exists()), None)\n",
    "if data_path is None:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError('Could not find data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv')\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(data_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "required = {'content_id', 'client_id', 'content_type', 'trend_direction'}\n",
    "missing_required = required - set(df.columns)\n",
    "if missing_required:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f'Missing required columns: {sorted(missing_required)}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Loaded:', data_path)\n",
    "print('Shape:', df.shape)\n",
    "print('Unique content IDs:', df['content_id'].nunique())\n",
    "print('Unique clients:', df['client_id'].nunique())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Build the feature vector\n",
    "\n",
    "The model vector uses content and historical activity fields that are available in the export. `trend_direction`, `trend_pct`, `is_declining_label`, IDs, and generation metadata are deliberately absent.\n",
    "\n",
    "Missing numeric values receive a median computed from the training data in a real split; this notebook uses the whole snapshot only to demonstrate construction. Missingness indicators are retained for fields whose absence is structural, especially keyword data and measured word count. Categorical values use an explicit `unknown` level."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# These are the approved model fields from scripts/ml_utils.py.\n",
    "numeric_features = [\n",
    "    'search_volume', 'competition', 'cpc', 'word_count', 'char_count',\n",
    "    'impressions_90d', 'clicks_90d', 'pageviews_90d', 'sessions_90d',\n",
    "    'users_90d', 'engaged_sessions_90d', 'ai_sessions_90d',\n",
    "    'scroll_events_90d', 'days_with_impressions', 'days_with_sessions',\n",
    "    'content_age_days', 'days_since_last_update', 'ctr', 'avg_position',\n",
    "    'engagement_rate', 'scroll_rate', 'ai_traffic_pct'\n",
    "]\n",
    "categorical_features = [\n",
    "    'competition_level', 'content_type', 'main_intent', 'age_tier',\n",
    "    'freshness_tier', 'word_count_tier', 'impression_tier', 'position_tier'\n",
    "]\n",
    "numeric_features = [c for c in numeric_features if c in df.columns]\n",
    "categorical_features = [c for c in categorical_features if c in df.columns]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Preserve structural missingness before filling.\n",
    "missing_flag_columns = [c for c in ['search_volume', 'competition', 'competition_level', 'cpc', 'word_count', 'char_count', 'main_intent'] if c in df.columns and df[c].isna().any()]\n",
    "X = pd.DataFrame(index=df.index)\n",
    "for col in numeric_features:\n",
    "    values = pd.to_numeric(df[col], errors='coerce').replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n",
    "    X[col] = values.fillna(values.median())\n",
    "for col in missing_flag_columns:\n",
    "    X[f'has_{col}'] = df[col].notna().astype('int8')\n",
    "for col in categorical_features:\n",
    "    X[col] = df[col].fillna('unknown').astype(str).replace({'': 'unknown', 'nan': 'unknown'})\n",
    "X = pd.get_dummies(X, columns=categorical_features, dtype='int8')\n",
    "\n",
    "assert not ({'trend_direction', 'trend_pct', 'is_declining_label', 'content_id', 'client_id'} & set(X.columns))\n",
    "print('Base numeric features:', numeric_features)\n",
    "print('Categorical features:', categorical_features)\n",
    "print('Missingness flags:', [c for c in X.columns if c.startswith('has_')])\n",
    "print('Feature matrix shape:', X.shape)\n",
    "print('Numeric matrix finite:', bool(np.isfinite(X.select_dtypes(include=np.number).to_numpy()).all()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Feature notes (meaning, missing, categorical, available-when?)\n",
    "\n",
    "The table below documents every base feature. The `available_before_label` column is intentionally conservative: the starter CSV is an export-time snapshot, so 90-day activity and derived rates overlap the period used to define the decline label. They are usable for export-time triage/classification, but not for claiming that the model predicts a later month. IDs and workflow metadata are context/excluded, not features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "feature_notes = {\n",
    "    'search_volume': ('Target-keyword demand estimate; missing when no keyword exists.', 'median + has flag', 'before export-time scoring; snapshot context'),\n    "    'competition': ('Keyword competition score from 0 to 1.', 'median + has flag', 'before export-time scoring; snapshot context'),\n    "    'cpc': ('Target-keyword cost-per-click estimate.', 'median + has flag', 'before export-time scoring; snapshot context'),\n    "    'word_count': ('Measured article word count.', 'median + has flag', 'before scoring if content is published'),\n    "    'char_count': ('Measured article character count.', 'median + has flag', 'before scoring if content is published'),\n    "    'impressions_90d': ('GSC impressions in the trailing 90 days.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'clicks_90d': ('GSC clicks in the trailing 90 days.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'pageviews_90d': ('GA4 pageviews in the trailing 90 days.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'sessions_90d': ('GA4 sessions in the trailing 90 days.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'users_90d': ('GA4 users in the trailing 90 days.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'engaged_sessions_90d': ('GA4 engaged sessions in the trailing 90 days.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'ai_sessions_90d': ('Sessions referred from AI tools, not citations.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'scroll_events_90d': ('GA4 scroll events in the trailing 90 days.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'days_with_impressions': ('Days with at least one GSC impression.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'days_with_sessions': ('Days with at least one GA4 session.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'content_age_days': ('Days since content creation.', 'median', 'before scoring'),\n    "    'days_since_last_update': ('Days since the last content update.', 'median', 'before scoring'),\n    "    'ctr': ('Clicks divided by impressions times 100; values are percentage points.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'avg_position': ('Mean GSC position; zero means no position data.', 'median; retain zero semantics in raw audit', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'engagement_rate': ('Engaged sessions divided by sessions times 100.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'scroll_rate': ('Scroll events divided by pageviews times 100; can exceed 100.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "    'ai_traffic_pct': ('AI sessions divided by sessions times 100; can exceed 100.', 'median', 'overlaps the label window'),\n    "}\n",
    "notes = pd.DataFrame([{'feature': c, 'meaning': feature_notes.get(c, ('Documented model feature', 'median', 'check dictionary'))[0], 'missing_handling': feature_notes.get(c, ('', '', ''))[1], 'available_before_label': feature_notes.get(c, ('', '', ''))[2]} for c in numeric_features])\n",
    "notes = pd.concat([notes, pd.DataFrame([{'feature': c, 'meaning': f'Categorical value: {c}.', 'missing_handling': 'unknown level', 'available_before_label': 'before export-time scoring'} for c in categorical_features])], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "print(notes.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print('All documented base features present:', set(notes['feature']) == set(numeric_features + categorical_features))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. The leakage hunt\n",
    "\n",
    "Three tests are required. First, the target and its direct source must not be in `X`. Second, any feature that is mathematically derived from the target inputs must be called out. Third, the 30-day columns must not be quietly treated as pre-label features: `trend_direction` compares `impressions_last_30d` with `impressions_prev_30d`, so both windows are label inputs. The same overlap warning applies to the 90-day snapshot metrics when the intended label is a future period."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "label = (df['trend_direction'].astype(str).str.lower() == 'down').astype('int8')\n",
    "direct_label_columns = {'trend_direction', 'trend_pct', 'is_declining_label'}\n",
    "label_input_columns = {'impressions_last_30d', 'impressions_prev_30d'}\n",
    "identity_columns = {'content_id', 'client_id'}\n",
    "workflow_columns = {'provider_used', 'model_used'}\n",
    "forbidden = direct_label_columns | identity_columns | workflow_columns\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Direct label columns present in X:', sorted(forbidden & set(X.columns)))\n",
    "print('Label-input columns present in X:', sorted(label_input_columns & set(X.columns)))\n",
    "print('Target prevalence:', round(float(label.mean()), 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "assert not (direct_label_columns & set(X.columns)), 'Direct label leakage found'\n",
    "assert not (identity_columns & set(X.columns)), 'Identifier leakage found'\n",
    "assert not (workflow_columns & set(X.columns)), 'Workflow/privacy leakage found'\n",
    "\n",
    "# A transparent audit table: direct leakage is a hard fail; overlapping windows are a design warning.\n",
    "leakage_audit = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {'item': 'target/direct derivatives', 'columns': sorted(direct_label_columns), 'status': 'PASS: excluded from X'},\n",
    "    {'item': 'target source windows', 'columns': sorted(label_input_columns), 'status': 'WARNING: do not use for future-month prediction'},\n",
    "    {'item': 'pseudonymous identifiers', 'columns': sorted(identity_columns), 'status': 'PASS: excluded from X'},\n",
    "    {'item': 'generation metadata', 'columns': sorted(workflow_columns), 'status': 'PASS: excluded from X'},\n",
    "])\n",
    "print(leakage_audit.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print('Conclusion: X is free of direct label, ID, and workflow leakage; temporal overlap must be respected in any future-window experiment.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. What I excluded and why\n",
    "\n",
    "The exclusions below are explicit rather than hidden in preprocessing. `trend_direction` and `trend_pct` define the outcome; the derived label is the target itself. The last/previous 30-day windows are retained in the raw dataset for diagnostics but excluded from this feature vector because they define the label and would be leakage for a future-period prediction. IDs support grouped validation only. Provider/model fields identify the generation workflow and may encode process or privacy information rather than page quality."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "excluded = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {'column': 'trend_direction', 'reason': 'Direct categorical source of the decline target.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'trend_pct', 'reason': 'Direct numeric calculation from the same windows used for the target.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'is_declining_label', 'reason': 'The target; never a predictor.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'impressions_last_30d', 'reason': 'Part of the target definition; overlaps the label window.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'impressions_prev_30d', 'reason': 'Part of the target definition; not a safe future-forecast feature in this snapshot.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'clicks_last_30d', 'reason': 'Recent-window metric; excluded to keep the static vector independent of the label window.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'clicks_prev_30d', 'reason': 'Recent comparison-window metric; excluded from the conservative vector.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'sessions_last_30d', 'reason': 'Recent-window metric; excluded to avoid temporal overlap.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'sessions_prev_30d', 'reason': 'Recent comparison-window metric; excluded from the conservative vector.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'content_id', 'reason': 'Pseudonymous identifier; context/grouping only.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'client_id', 'reason': 'Pseudonymous identifier; use for grouped splits, never as a feature.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'provider_used', 'reason': 'Generation workflow metadata; unstable and potentially privacy/process revealing.'},\n",
    "    {'column': 'model_used', 'reason': 'Generation workflow metadata; unstable and not a page-quality feature.'},\n",
    "])\n",
    "print(excluded.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print('Excluded columns found in raw data:', sorted(set(excluded['column']) & set(df.columns)))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Self-check\n",
    "\n",
    "- [x] Every section is filled in order: vector, feature notes, leakage hunt, exclusions, and this self-check.\n",
    "- [x] The feature matrix is built from named numeric/categorical fields with explicit fills and missingness flags.\n",
    "- [x] IDs, the target, target-derived fields, recent label windows, and workflow metadata are not silently used.\n",
    "- [x] Missingness is audited as a pattern, not treated as random.\n",
    "- [x] The temporal limitation is stated honestly: this snapshot supports export-time triage, not a claim about a future month.\n",
    "- [x] The notebook ends with executable assertions that fail if direct leakage enters `X`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "checks = {\n",
    "    'data_loaded': len(df) > 0,\n",
    "    'feature_matrix_nonempty': X.shape[1] > 0,\n",
    "    'no_direct_label_leakage': not (direct_label_columns & set(X.columns)),\n",
    "    'no_identifier_leakage': not (identity_columns & set(X.columns)),\n",
    "    'no_workflow_metadata': not (workflow_columns & set(X.columns)),\n",
    "    'all_numeric_values_finite': bool(np.isfinite(X.select_dtypes(include=np.number).to_numpy()).all()),\n",
    "    'all_base_features_documented': set(notes['feature']) == set(numeric_features + categorical_features),\n",
    "    'target_is_binary': set(label.unique()).issubset({0, 1}),\n",
    "}\n",
    "for name, passed in checks.items():\n",
    "    print(f'{name}: {passed}')\n",
    "assert all(checks.values()), 'One or more notebook self-checks failed.'\n",
    "print('All self-checks passed.')"
   ]
  }
 ],
